{"title":"1988 AJHSME Problems/Problem 17","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The shaded region formed by the two intersecting perpendicular rectangles, in square units, is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/addd68de53329242c875ed0d9bdfcc9127497b92.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] fill((0,0)--(6,0)--(6,-3.5)--(9,-3.5)--(9,0)--(10,0)--(10,2)--(9,2)--(9,4.5)--(6,4.5)--(6,2)--(0,2)--cycle,black); label(&quot;2&quot;,(0,.9),W); label(&quot;3&quot;,(7.3,4.5),N); draw((0,-3.3)--(0,-5.3),linewidth(1)); draw((0,-4.3)--(3.7,-4.3),linewidth(1)); label(&quot;10&quot;,(4.7,-3.7),S); draw((5.7,-4.3)--(10,-4.3),linewidth(1)); draw((10,-3.3)--(10,-5.3),linewidth(1)); draw((11,4.5)--(13,4.5),linewidth(1)); draw((12,4.5)--(12,2),linewidth(1)); label(&quot;8&quot;,(11.3,1),E); draw((12,0)--(12,-3.5),linewidth(1)); draw((11,-3.5)--(13,-3.5),linewidth(1)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"198\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/1/a61990a818524f2371a0a3a9141f09c03e7e0535.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 23 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 38 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 44 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 46 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ \\text{unable to be determined from the information given}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"739\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The area of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/5/bd5f45a42f018df670ff996942e107e15312ce69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" /> rectangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, while the area of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/3/a1376df593af114887920fa973b68c9087cf6c5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8 \\times 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> rectangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.  If these two areas were added together, however, the area of the intersection, which is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/3/a832b76c4f4a4ec13ac1b557da4fed6006e64d00.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> rectangle, would be counted twice.  Since the intersection has area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the area of this figure must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/4/9b4f212c888deb0b398c1c1930781074add6733b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20 + 24 - 6 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ 38}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"179\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table cl